+## V20-O-R-I isolated PostgreSQL 17 creator membership
+
+This source-only candidate adds one laboratory profile to exact V20-O-R.
+The profile exists only with the fixed synthetic limited actor issuer in the
+owned fixture. The issuer creates the actors through its actual PostgreSQL
+17 session with `createrole_self_grant` empty. Each actor keeps its direct
+native ACLs and has one incoming creator edge and zero outgoing edges.
+The exact incoming row has the actor as roleid, the separate non-superuser
+issuer as member, and the fixture bootstrap superuser (OID 10) as grantor.
+Only ADMIN is true. Both issuer and grantor role identities enter the held
+catalog seal. The complete actor/owner membership inventory remains sealed.
+Without the synthetic issuer, the original no-membership rule applies.
+
+The fixture verifies the edges and owner separation independently before
+capturing catalog gold. The added case submits and commits one original
+Install as the real actor, reads it from the independent reader, then checks
+that the issuer cannot assume or administer either owner. An extra inert
+incoming grant and an extra SET-only outgoing grant each deny the actor and
+the independent read under the existing catalog digest. Removing the
+synthetic fault restores the exact reply and committed rows. The socket
+fixture supplies genuine role sessions within the disposable server, with
+no SCRAM, expiry, managed issuer, rotation, terminal or hosted readiness
+claim. All 43 V20-O-R methods, eight table declarations, fixed anchor broker
+and policy bytes are preserved. Separate native review and execution remain
+required for this source candidate.
